 financings in both the private and public markets, and other corporate finance transactions. The FR segment advises debtors, creditors, and other parties-in-interest related to recapitalization/deleveraging transactions. This segment also provides a range of advisory services, such as structuring, negotiation, and confirmation of plans of reorganization; structuring and analysis of exchange offers; liability management transactions; corporate viability assessment; dispute resolution and expert testimony; and procuring debtor-in-possession financing. The FVA segment provides valuation services to companies; debt and equity interests comprising illiquid investments; and other assets and liabilities. This segment also offers fairness opinions in connection with mergers and acquisitions and other transactions; solvency opinions in connection with corporate spin-offs and dividend recapitalizations; other types of financial opinions; and diligence, tax, transaction accounting, and other financial advisory services, as well as dispute resolution services. It serves corporations, financial sponsors, and government agencies. Houlihan Lokey, Inc. was incorporated in 1972 and is headquartered in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott Joseph Adelson | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $13.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $935K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $244K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $72K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Houlihan Lokey, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $9.2B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 34% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 24-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The business throws off $682M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.65\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Helia Group (ASX:HLI): The Housing Signals That Matter Most Now","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/value/helia-group-asxhli-the-housing-signals-that-matter-most-now","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795153440.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Helia Group (ASX:HLI) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock on the Radar?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/financial/helia-group-asxhli-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-on-the-radar-1","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1794977340.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.374,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Helia Group (ASX:HLI): Why Its Earnings Multiple Stays Modest","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/value/helia-group-asxhli-why-its-earnings-multiple-stays-modest","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794901080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"5,559 Houlihan Lokey, Inc. $HLI Shares Acquired by Diversified Trust Co","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/5559-houlihan-lokey-inc-hli-shares-acquire